{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The protected observation `y` is a top-level data variable and is observed exactly once with a plain built-in sampling statement. Context data (`M`, `N`, `x0`, and `X`) are used only as sizes/covariates, and all parameters have built-in prior sampling statements before they are used in the likelihood.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> M; // Number of covariates
  int<lower=0> N; // Number of observations

  vector[M] x0;   // Covariate baselines
  matrix[N, M] X; // Covariate design matrix

  array[N] real y;      // Variates
}

transformed data {
  matrix[N, M] deltaX;
  for (n in 1:N) {
    deltaX[n,] = X[n] - x0';
  }
}

parameters {
  real alpha;          // Intercept
  vector[M] beta;      // Slopes
  real<lower=0> nu_inv; // Inverse degrees of freedom
  real<lower=0> sigma; // Measurement Variability
}

model {
  // Prior model
  alpha ~ normal(0, 10);
  beta ~ normal(0, 10);
  nu_inv ~ normal(0, 0.5);
  sigma ~ normal(0, 5);

  // Vectorized observation model
  y ~ student_t(inv(nu_inv), alpha + deltaX * beta, sigma);
}

// Simulate a full observation from the current value of the parameters
generated quantities {
  array[N] real y_pred = student_t_rng(inv(nu_inv), alpha + deltaX * beta, sigma);
}
